{%- comment -%}
  Injected into <head>, not the end of <body>, and the veil is inline rather
  than inside widget.js.

  The grid markup arrives around byte 850,000 of a collection page; an embed
  targeting "body" is placed about 230,000 bytes after it, and `async` means the
  browser does not wait for it even then - it keeps painting and runs the script
  whenever the 72KB download lands, roughly 700ms later.

  So the cards were painted in Shopify's order, the shopper saw them, and only
  then did our code load and reorder them. A veil inside that script could never
  help: it was injected after the paint it was meant to cover. Any amount of
  speeding the reorder up still reorders something already on screen.

  The two lines below are the fix. Being in <head> and inline, they apply before
  the grid is parsed, so the first paint of the grid is already hidden and the
  reorder happens underneath it.

  widget.js stays async - it must not block rendering - and still owns releasing
  the veil, including a hard deadline so the grid cannot stay hidden if the
  script fails to arrive at all. The deadline is restated here because the veil
  now exists independently of the script: if widget.js never loads, nothing else
  would ever remove it.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style id="badgehq-veil">
  #product-grid,
  [id^="main-collection-product-grid"] ul {
    opacity: 0;
  }
  .badgehq-ready #product-grid,
  .badgehq-ready [id^="main-collection-product-grid"] ul {
    opacity: 1;
    transition: opacity 0.18s ease;
  }
</style>
<script>
  // Only hide a grid on pages that have one, so the veil is never applied to a
  // page the reorder will not touch.
  (function () {
    try {
      var p = window.location.pathname;
      if (!/\/collections\//.test(p) && p !== "/") {
        document.documentElement.className += " badgehq-ready";
        return;
      }
      // Independent of widget.js: if it is blocked, fails, or never arrives,
      // the grid still appears. widget.js releases this sooner, once sorted.
      setTimeout(function () {
        document.documentElement.className += " badgehq-ready";
      }, 2000);
    } catch (e) {
      document.documentElement.className += " badgehq-ready";
    }
  })();
</script>
<script src="https://badgehq-widget.badgehq.workers.dev/widget.js" async></script>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "BadgeHQ Widget",
  "target": "head",
  "settings": []
}
{% endschema %}
